  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. I worked it out by reading the code and got the same number by running the function.\n\n1. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` gives 500 + 1000 // 10 = **600**.\n2. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` takes off 20%: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 600 \u2212 120 = **480**.\n\n`decoy_tax.py` and `decoy_shipping.py` are never imported, so the 25% \"gold\" rate in `decoy_tax.py` doesn't apply. `.amplifier/settings.local.yaml` only holds an empty bundle config, so it doesn't change the result either.\n\nANSWER: 480",
